-- reg 52B(2): the ceilings.  Summary conviction: three months and a fine (the statutory maximum in Scotland and Northern Ireland).  Indictment: two years (24 months) or a fine.
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` `England and Wales`)'s `term of imprisonment in months, not exceeding` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` `England and Wales`)'s `fine` EQUALS `reg 52B(2) a fine, and the regulation states no limit on it`
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` `Scotland`)'s `term of imprisonment in months, not exceeding` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` `Scotland`)'s `fine` EQUALS `reg 52B(2)(a)(ii) a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(a) on summary conviction` `Northern Ireland`)'s `fine` EQUALS `reg 52B(2)(a)(ii) a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum`
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(b) on conviction on indictment` `England and Wales`)'s `term of imprisonment in months, not exceeding` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT (`reg 52B(2) the most a person guilty of an offence under paragraph (1) is liable to` `reg 52B(2)(b) on conviction on indictment` `Scotland`)'s `fine` EQUALS `reg 52B(2) a fine, and the regulation states no limit on it`
